**Holiday Policy Overview**

| Item | Details |
|------|---------|
| **Public Holidays** | The company observes **12 official public holidays** each year. The full holiday calendar is published by HR at the start of the year. |
| **Compensatory Leave** | If you’re scheduled to work on a public holiday, you’re eligible for a compensatory day off. |
| **Annual Paid Leave** | Full‑time employees receive **20 days of paid annual leave** per calendar year. |
| **Advance Notice** | Submit leave requests through the HR portal **at least 5 working days** before the intended start date. |
| **Carry‑Forward** | Unused annual leave can roll over to the next year, but only **up to 5 days**. |
| **Sick Leave** | Separate from annual leave: **10 paid sick days** per year. A medical certificate is required for absences longer than 2 consecutive days. |

**Quick Tips**

- Check the holiday calendar early in the year so you can plan vacations around the public holidays.
- If you need to work on a holiday, just let your manager know and you’ll get the compensatory day off.
- Remember to submit your leave requests on time to avoid any last‑minute hiccups.

If you have any more questions—whether it’s about how to request leave, or anything else—just let me know! 🌟'
